snippet.textDisplay:
@arcticgalegamer8139 Yeah that's not the point I was making. In an ambush position, or just standing "guard" do you really think the Russians (in this case) are gonna go stumbling around in boxes, or doing cartwheels during patrol missions especially while potentially being watched by drones operated by real people, sniper or just evading mines and other traps ?

IED's was a big problem in Afghanistan, while not automated they where still a threat even while soldiers where aware of them and sometimes could see them for 10's of meters, even just a bag on the side of a street or a recently digged on spot would alert soldiers. 

What do you think getting shot at any time by something without a thermal signal that is easy to hide is gonna do to people ?

